<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joash of Judah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 9th – early 8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Jehoash of Judah · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-david">House of David</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joash, also called Jehoash, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> in the late 9th and early 8th centuries BCE. According to the Bible he was hidden as an infant when his grandmother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athaliah">Athaliah</a> killed the royal family, and crowned at the age of seven by the priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoiada">Jehoiada</a>. He repaired the temple in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> but bought off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazael">Hazael</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> with its treasures, and was murdered by his own officials.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joash-of-judah.jpg" alt="Joash of Judah" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joas_of_Judah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…ruled throughout by kings of the House of David, an unusual stability compared with the frequent coups in the northern kingdom; the only break was the six-year rule of Queen Athaliah, daughter of the house of Omri, which ended when priests placed her grandson <b>Joash</b> on the throne.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Kingdom of Judah · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
